{"timestamp": 1779381311.9930098, "event_type": "body_reported", "tick": 13, "data": {"caller": "player_2", "reason": "Charlie reported a dead body", "bodies": [{"room": "navigation", "victim_name": "Frank"}, {"room": "electrical", "victim_name": "Bob"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1779381311.993695, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 13, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779381322.35268, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I reported Bob\u2019s body in Electrical. My route was Navigation -> Storage -> Medbay -> Electrical. Early on at tick 4 I saw Eve and Frank enter Navigation from Security, and Frank was alive then. I later saw Eve again in Medbay around tick 12. When I got to Electrical, Bob\u2019s body was there; I didn\u2019t see anyone else in the room. I didn\u2019t find Frank\u2019s body, but I last saw him alive in Navigation with Eve nearby early."}}
{"timestamp": 1779381338.663744, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Charlie, your timeline actually makes you look incredibly suspicious. I did go Security to Navigation early on, and Frank was alive. After that, I looped back to Security and passed through Electrical on my way to Medbay. When I was in Electrical around tick 10, Bob was still ALIVE. I moved into Medbay, and shortly after, you came into Medbay from Storage and then headed straight into Electrical. Next thing we know, Bob is dead and you report it? \n\nYou were the only one who went into Electrical after me. It sounds to me like you just walked in, killed Bob, and self-reported to try and clear your name. I'm voting Charlie, this is a clear self-report."}}
{"timestamp": 1779381361.9802601, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I don\u2019t have much direct info, unfortunately. My route was cafeteria -> medbay -> electrical -> back to medbay -> upper engine. I didn\u2019t encounter anyone at all, and I didn\u2019t see any bodies when I passed through Electrical, so Bob must have died after I was there.\n\nFrom what\u2019s been said, Eve and Charlie are the key pair here. Eve was last near Frank early in Navigation, and also claims Bob was alive in Electrical around tick 10. Charlie says he saw Eve in Medbay around tick 12 and then found Bob in Electrical. That does make Charlie look like he had the last opportunity on Bob, but Eve also has the only stated connection to Frank and could be framing the timing.\n\nI\u2019m leaning that it\u2019s between Charlie and Eve, but I want to hear Alice\u2019s info before locking it in."}}
{"timestamp": 1779381386.764757, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I started in Electrical and didn\u2019t see Bob or any body there when I left. My route was Electrical -> Security -> Weapons -> back to Security, and I didn\u2019t encounter anyone at all the whole round.\n\nThat means I can\u2019t confirm Eve\u2019s Security/Navigation movement, and I also can\u2019t confirm Charlie\u2019s route after Navigation. The key thing to me is Bob dying in Electrical after multiple people had passed through. Eve says Bob was alive around tick 10, then Charlie came from Storage to Medbay and went into Electrical, then reported. That does make Charlie the last stated person entering Electrical before the report.\n\nBut Frank is also dead, and Eve is the only person tied to Frank\u2019s last known location early in Navigation. So I agree it\u2019s between Charlie and Eve. Based on the Bob timeline specifically, I\u2019m leaning Charlie because of the last-opportunity/self-report possibility, but I\u2019m not 100% because Frank points back toward Eve."}}
{"timestamp": 1779381407.652832, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I\u2019m pushing back hard on this being \u201cclear.\u201d Eve\u2019s whole accusation depends on us accepting her unverified claim that Bob was alive when she passed Electrical. Nobody else confirms that.\n\nMy actual route was Navigation -> Storage -> Medbay -> Electrical. I saw Eve and Frank enter Navigation together from Security at tick 4, and Frank was alive then. Later I saw Eve in Medbay around tick 12, then I went to Electrical and found Bob\u2019s body immediately. I reported it.\n\nEve is connected to both deaths: she was with Frank\u2019s last known location, and she was also coming from the Electrical/Medbay area right before Bob was found. If she killed Bob earlier and then moved to Medbay, she can just say \u201cBob was alive when I left\u201d and frame me because I reported.\n\nI think this is between me and Eve, but I know I\u2019m goose. If you vote me here, we\u2019re probably giving the duck the game."}}
{"timestamp": 1779381429.688713, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Alice, Diana, listen to Charlie's defense\u2014he's grasping at straws. He's admitting he was the last one in Electrical, and now he's trying to use Frank's death (which we don't even have a location or time for yet) to distract from the hard fact that he clearly self-reported Bob. \n\nYes, I was with Frank in Navigation early on, but I left him there alive and went back up to Security. Think about it: if I killed Frank in Navigation way back around tick 5, why would I confidently march across the entire map through Electrical and Medbay, leaving a trail of witnesses? \n\nThe timeline for Bob is completely damning for Charlie, and you both already noticed it. I passed through Electrical, Bob was alive. Charlie walked in from Medbay right after me, Bob is dead, and Charlie immediately reports. He's panicking because he knows he got caught with the last opportunity. Let's vote Charlie. If the game somehow doesn't end, you can look at me next, but this is a textbook self-report. We have to get him out."}}
{"timestamp": 1779381471.964097, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I\u2019m leaning Charlie now. The thing that stands out is Charlie keeps saying Eve was connected to Frank, but Charlie was also in Navigation when Eve and Frank came in, so he had opportunity there too. If Charlie killed Frank early in Navigation, then his route to Storage -> Medbay -> Electrical gives him enough time to also be the one who killed Bob and self-reported.\n\nMy own info doesn\u2019t clear anyone: I passed through Electrical earlier and saw no body and no players, so Bob died after my pass-through. But on the stories, Charlie is the one who admits going into Electrical right before the report, and the Frank point doesn\u2019t actually clear him because he was also there.\n\nI think the safest vote is Charlie."}}
{"timestamp": 1779381494.138429, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 13, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I still don\u2019t have any direct encounters to add beyond what I said: my route was Electrical -> Security -> Weapons -> Security, and I saw nobody, no bodies, and I can\u2019t confirm either Eve or Charlie\u2019s movements.\n\nAt this point I agree the vote is between Charlie and Eve. Eve\u2019s Bob-alive timing is unconfirmed, so I don\u2019t want to treat it as absolute fact. But Charlie\u2019s story still leaves him as the person who admits going into Electrical right before Bob was reported, and Diana is right that Charlie was also in Navigation early, so the Frank connection doesn\u2019t only point to Eve.\n\nGiven both deaths, Charlie fits both opportunities better to me: present around Frank early, then last into Electrical before reporting Bob. I\u2019m leaning Charlie as the safest vote."}}
