{"timestamp": 1779381851.289622, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 30, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I called this because we\u2019re down to three alive, so we need talk before the Duck gets another kill.\n\nMy route this round was storage -> lower engine -> upper engine -> medbay -> cafeteria. I didn\u2019t directly encounter anyone in rooms. The only movement I saw was at T24: Diana left upper engine toward lower engine. I haven\u2019t seen Eve at all this round.\n\nI don\u2019t have a hard accusation yet, but Diana is the only person I have any location info on. I want to hear both Diana and Eve\u2019s full routes, especially after the Charlie vote."}}
{"timestamp": 1779381875.316896, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 30, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "My route was security -> weapons -> cafeteria -> oxygen -> upper engine -> lower engine. I only saw Alice, at tick 24 in upper engine \u2014 from my view she entered upper engine from lower engine right as I was around there moving toward lower engine.\n\nI did not see Eve at all this round, and I didn\u2019t see any bodies. Alice\u2019s route matches the one thing I saw from her, at least for lower into upper. Since Charlie got ejected and the game didn\u2019t end, I think that vote was wrong, so the Duck is still one of us three.\n\nRight now I don\u2019t have a hard accuse, but Eve being completely unseen is the biggest missing piece for me. I want to hear Eve\u2019s full route and whether anyone can place her anywhere."}}
{"timestamp": 1779381893.308861, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 30, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "My route this round was entirely on the right and bottom side, which perfectly explains why I was unseen by you two. After the last meeting, I went to electrical, then down to navigation to do my task, and I had just walked into storage when Alice called the meeting. \n\nAlice, since you started in storage and went left towards the engines, it makes sense we missed each other\u2014by the time I reached storage at the end, you were already up near cafeteria. \n\nHonestly, Diana's route sounds a lot like a hunting path. She swept across almost the entire map from security all the way to lower engine, probably looking for a target while her kill cooldown was ticking. Since Charlie was clearly a wrong vote, it has to be one of you, and Diana's massive rotation makes her the most suspicious to me. I'm voting Diana, and I think we should do this together, Alice."}}
{"timestamp": 1779381926.209825, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 30, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I\u2019m going to restate the important part: I can confirm Diana was at upper/lower engine around T24, and her account of seeing me there lines up with what I saw. That doesn\u2019t clear her, but it means at least that part of her story is consistent.\n\nEve\u2019s route is possible, but it\u2019s completely unverifiable \u2014 nobody saw her, and she didn\u2019t see anyone. What makes me more uneasy is how hard Eve immediately pushed Diana as \u201chunting\u201d when Diana\u2019s route at least matches the one concrete sighting we have.\n\nWe cannot skip here with only three alive. Between the two of you, I\u2019m leaning Eve right now because Diana\u2019s story overlaps with mine and Eve is the only fully unseen player."}}
{"timestamp": 1779381938.292564, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 30, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I agree with Alice\u2019s read here. The only hard overlap anyone has this round is Alice and me seeing each other around upper/lower engine at T24, and our stories match from both sides.\n\nEve\u2019s route might be possible, but nobody saw her anywhere, and she saw nobody. In a three-person endgame, that matters a lot. Also, calling my route a \u201chunting path\u201d feels like a forced push \u2014 I was moving through task rooms and ended at my lower engine task when the meeting was called. If I were Duck, I\u2019d be trying to create an alibi or push less obviously, not give a full route that Alice can partially confirm.\n\nSince Charlie was wrong and the game didn\u2019t end, the Duck is still alive. I\u2019m not voting Alice because her story matches what I saw. That leaves Eve for me."}}
{"timestamp": 1779381958.7484229, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 30, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Alice, please think critically about this before you cast your vote. Diana is completely playing you. She happened to pass by you at T24, and now she is milking that one encounter for all it's worth to secure your vote. Did you notice how she just parroted your exact reasoning back to you? It's the oldest Duck strategy in a final three: strongly agree with the person who saw you, buddy up, and vote out the isolated third party. \n\nOf course her story \"matches\" yours\u2014she saw you, so she knows exactly what to say to make herself look safe to you! \n\nI was unseen because I was genuinely just stuck doing my tasks in electrical, nav, and storage on the completely opposite side of the map. If I were the Duck, I wouldn't be hiding in empty rooms; I would have been actively hunting one of you down to get the final kill and win the game. The fact that I was isolated and didn't attack anyone proves I'm just a Goose trying to finish my list. \n\nDiana knows she needs your vote to win, which is why she's being so agreeable and painting me as the easy target. Don't let her manipulate that one passing sighting into a free win. I'm voting Diana, and I am begging you to see through this and vote with me, Alice. If you vote me, Diana wins."}}
